        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Today marks the 89th anniversary of the Marco Polo Bridge Incident and 70th anniversary of the Huang Fu Hsing branch. Chair Cheng, along side with KMT elected officials, attended the ceremony to commemorate the history.\n\n89 years ago, the Marco Polo Bridge Incident marked the beginning of the War of Resistance, eight years in which countless soldiers and civilians gave their lives to defend their homeland. That war engulfed East Asia, Southeast Asia, and the Pacific, which left profound suffering across the region. 70 years ago, the Huang Fu Hsing branch was founded to honor those who served, and generations of veterans have carried that spirit of duty and sacrifice ever since.\n\nWe remember this history with gratitude to those who defended the nation, and with a clear-eyed view of today’s security environment, one in which we cannot ignore the growing tensions across the Taiwan Strait and throughout the Indo-Pacific. The lessons of the Second World War still resonate. Our responsibility is to prevent another devastating conflict and to choose the path of peace.\n\nTaiwan has an important role to play, and so does the Kuomintang. By remembering history with honesty, and working to preserve peace, we hope to ensure that future generations never again endure the tragedies of war. 🕊️"
        },
